  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& f\\left(0^{-}\\right)=\\mathrm{e}^{\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{\\mathrm{ax}}{\\mathrm{x}}}=\\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{a}} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{f}(0)=1+\\mathrm{b} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{f}\\left(0^{+}\\right)=\\frac{\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{\\mathrm{x}+4}}}{\\frac{1}{3}(\\mathrm{x}+\\mathrm{c})^{-\\frac{2}{3}}}=\\frac{\\frac{1}{2(2)}}{\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\mathrm{c}^{-\\frac{2}{3}}} \\\\\n& =\\frac{3}{4} \\mathrm{c}^{2 / 3}<br/>\\end{aligned}$<br/>Also at $\\mathrm{x}=0$;<br/>$c^{1 / 3}=2 \\Rightarrow c=8$<br/>So $\\mathrm{f}\\left(0^{+}\\right)=\\frac{3}{4}(8)^{2 / 3}=3$<br/>Now, $\\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{a}}=\\mathrm{b}+1=3$<br/>$\\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{a}} . \\mathrm{b} \\cdot \\mathrm{c}=3 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 8=48$",
    "image": null
  },
